Z||000004||FormulaJoe||12-29-2001||10:00 AM||||Check out: <A HREF="http://www.dal.net" TARGET=_blank>www.dal.net</A> <BR>has the history and whatnot.  There is a java client there for accessing the network but I use a small client called ircle (Mac).  There is a windows client called mIRC, very popular, should be a link off the main page for downloading it .  IRC (internet relay chat) was one of the first protocols after email (I think, could be wrong here) to come along, way back in the day.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Was originally a small fast way of talking to people around the world and for the most part has stayed true to that beginning.  I prefer it to all the "instant" messaging, with its competing protocols and bloated code, but that is just me.<P>------------------<BR>Yellow Formula<BR>(soon to be 3.4 DOHC)||||reg||6
